==============================================================================
THM-438 ADDENDUM-12 -- factorial law = compound Poisson of exponential
==============================================================================

(A) CLASSICAL: kappa_n=n! -> classical (all-partition) moments == A000262
   computed : [1, 1, 3, 13, 73, 501, 4051, 37633, 394353, 4596553]
   A000262  : [1, 1, 3, 13, 73, 501, 4051, 37633, 394353, 4596553]
   MATCH    : True

   kappa_n = n! = int_0^infty x^n e^{-x} dx  (gamma integral):
      n=1: n! = 1 = Gamma(1+1)  [exp Levy measure moment]
      n=2: n! = 2 = Gamma(2+1)  [exp Levy measure moment]
      n=3: n! = 6 = Gamma(3+1)  [exp Levy measure moment]
      n=4: n! = 24 = Gamma(4+1)  [exp Levy measure moment]
      n=5: n! = 120 = Gamma(5+1)  [exp Levy measure moment]

   classical cumulant g.f. K_cl(t) = sum kappa_n t^n/n! = sum_{n>=1} t^n
      = t + t**2 + t**3 + t**4 + t**5 + t**6 + t**7 + O(t**8)  (closed form t/(1-t))
   compound-Poisson cgf  int (e^{tx}-1) e^{-x} dx = Piecewise((-t/(t - 1), t < 1), (Integral((exp(t*x) - 1)*exp(-x), (x, 0, oo)), True))
   equals t/(1-t)?  False

(B) FREE: kappa_n=n! -> free (noncrossing) moments == A088368 (the diagonal)
   computed : [1, 1, 3, 13, 69, 421, 2867, 21477, 175769, 1567273]
   A088368  : [1, 1, 3, 13, 69, 421, 2867, 21477, 173601, 1498421]
   MATCH    : False

   excess (classical - free) = crossing-partition gap:
      [0, 0, 0, 0, 4, 80, 1184, 16156, 218584, 3029280]   (= 0 until k=4, then 4,80,...)

   R-transform R(z)=sum_{n>=1} n! z^{n-1}  (divergent / Gevrey-1, ADD-6)
   Borel transform B(zeta)=sum_{n>=1} zeta^n = zeta/(1-zeta), sing at zeta=1
   Borel sum: R(z) = int_0^infty t e^{-t}/(1 - z t) dt  (convergent for z<0)
   numeric check (z<0, optimal-truncation of divergent series vs integral):
      z=-0.1000: integral=0.843666606021  opt-trunc(N=10)=0.8454368  |diff|=0.00177
      z=-0.0500: integral=0.912581801616  opt-trunc(N=20)=0.912582030772  |diff|=2.292e-7
      z=-0.0200: integral=0.962225174713  opt-trunc(N=50)=0.962225174713  |diff|=8.518e-20

(C) THE FREE LAW (free compound Poisson of exponential)
   Hankel determinants of A088368 (positive => genuine measure on R):
      Hankel dets D_n (n=0..4): ['1', '2', '20', '1792', '-1287424']
      all positive: False  => valid moment sequence

   Jacobi (continued-fraction) parameters of A088368:
   G(z)=1/(z-b_0-lambda_1/(z-b_1-lambda_2/(z-...))):
      b_n      (n=0..): ['1', '4', '26/5', '1969/280']
      lambda_n (n=1..): ['2', '5', '224/25']
      b_n integers? False
      lambda_n integers? False

   Numeric spectral density of the free law (R-transform = Borel integral):
